    {
      "id": "payroll_1164_721632",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3718.312343720521,
      "y": 4433.201491248349,
      "width": 624,
      "height": 93,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#7c2d12",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a001165",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 8354,
      "version": 80,
      "versionNonce": 603252315,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788412268113,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 11.5,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "1. Create a Payrun by choosing Salary Structure and payroll Period.\n2. Compute generates/updates the employee payslips in that Payrun.\n3. Review warnings before validation (examples in the source: A/C missing, duplicate payslip).\n4. Validate / mark payroll as paid when ready.\n5. Each payslip can generate a printable PDF.\n6. The Payrun provides the bulk Send Payslips action so employees receive their payslip by email.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Create a Payrun by choosing Salary Structure and payroll Period.\n2. Compute generates/updates the employee payslips in that Payrun.\n3. Review warnings before validation (examples in the source: A/C missing, duplicate payslip).\n4. Validate / mark payroll as paid when ready.\n5. Each payslip can generate a printable PDF.\n6. The Payrun provides the bulk Send Payslips action so employees receive their payslip by email.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
