      "seed": 8692,
      "version": 80,
      "versionNonce": 1210449883,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788412269777,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 11.5,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "• A Salary Structure is a named collection of Salary Rules (example from the source: Regular Salary).\n• Structure Form should show the included rules and their sequence.\n• Rule List/Form should expose Rule Name, Code, Category, Salary Structure and Sequence.\n• The source shows computation choices such as Fixed Amount, Percentage of Wage and Python Code.\n• Categories distinguish components such as Basic, Allowance, Gross, Deduction and Net.\n• These rules are what populate the Salary Computation section of the employee Payslip.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• A Salary Structure is a named collection of Salary Rules (example from the source: Regular Salary).\n• Structure Form should show the included rules and their sequence.\n• Rule List/Form should expose Rule Name, Code, Category, Salary Structure and Sequence.\n• The source shows computation choices such as Fixed Amount, Percentage of Wage and Python Code.\n• Categories distinguish components such as Basic, Allowance, Gross, Deduction and Net.\n• These rules are what populate the Salary Computation section of the employee Payslip.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "payroll_1503_485815",
